{"id":"n1-240","title":"～折に (〜ori ni)","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Indicates the time or occasion when something happens; 'when', 'at the time of'.","longExplanation":"The ～折に grammar point is used in a somewhat formal register to express that one event or action takes place on the occasion of another. It essentially means 'when' or 'at the time of'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + 折に, Verb-た形 + 折に, Noun + の折に","examples":[{"jp":"父が病気の折に、私は留学していました。","romaji":"Chichi ga byouki no ori ni, watashi wa ryuugaku shite imashita.","en":"When my father was ill, I was studying abroad.","words":[{"surface":"父","vocabId":"1497610","reading":"ちち"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"病気","vocabId":"1490230","reading":"びょうき"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"折","vocabId":"1385780","reading":"おり"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"私","vocabId":"1311110","reading":"わたし"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"留学","vocabId":"1552740","reading":"りゅうがく"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5]},{"jp":"日本へ行く折に、お土産を買ってきてください。","romaji":"Nihon e iku ori ni, omiyage o katte kite kudasai.","en":"When you go to Japan, please buy souvenirs.","words":[{"surface":"日本","vocabId":"1582710","reading":"にほん"},{"surface":"へ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"行く","vocabId":"1578850","reading":"いく"},{"surface":"折","vocabId":"1385780","reading":"おり"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"お","vocabId":null},{"surface":"土産","vocabId":"1445360","reading":"みやげ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"買っ","vocabId":"1473740","reading":"かう","baseForm":"買う"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"き","vocabId":"1221520","reading":"き","baseForm":"